==Icelandic==

===Etymology===
From late {{etyl|non|is}} {{m|non|reikna}}, which is borrowed from {{cog|gml|rekenen}}, which is cognate to Dutch {{m|nl|rekenen}}, English {{m|en|reckon}} and German {{m|de|rechnen}}.<ref>''rekna''; in: [[w:en:Alf Torp|Alf Torp]], "Nynorsk Etymologisk Ordbok", Oslo 1992 (reprint), {{ISBN|82-90520-17-4}}</ref>

===Verb===
{{is-verb|reiknaði|reiknað}}
# {{lb|is|ambitransitive|governs the accusative}} to [[calculate]], to [[compute]]

====Derived terms====
* {{l|is|reikna út|reikna eitthvað út}} (to calculate something, to work something out)
* {{l|is|reiknast}}
* {{l|is|reikna með|reikna með einhverju}} (to expect something, to reckon on something)

